.TH QFW_RUN_ALL.SH 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Examples"
.SH NAME
qfw_run_all.sh \- run the backend-compatible QFw example suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_run_all.sh [options]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw_run_all.sh
runs compatible examples sequentially and verifies that each completed wrapper
emits a successful terminal result. It continues after individual failures,
prints a pass, fail, and skip summary, and returns nonzero when any selected
test fails.
.PP
Local mode gives each backend-aware wrapper its own application-owned service
lifecycle. Site mode connects every compatible wrapper to the existing site
directory and QPM. MPI smoke remains a separate command because it validates
a specialized MPI service and task-placement contract.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --service-mode " mode"
Select
.B local
or
.BR site .
The default is
.BR local .
.TP
.BI --backend " name"
Select the backend used by compatible tests. The default is
.BR nwqsim .
Real IQM requires site mode.
.TP
.BI --site-config " path"
Override the activated site configuration for a site-mode run.
.TP
.BI --runtime-config " path"
Override the runtime selected by the service mode. Normal local and site runs
use installed profiles and do not require this option.
.TP
.BI --tests " list"
Run a comma-separated subset. Valid names are
.BR init-test ,
.BR shim-smoke ,
.BR qiskit-simple ,
.BR ghz-qiskit ,
.BR ghz-pennylane ,
.BR pennylane ,
.BR qaoa ,
.BR qiskit-vqe ,
.BR supermarq ,
and
.BR chemistry .
.TP
.B --verbose
Enable shell tracing in the selected wrappers.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print command help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QFW_RUN_ALL_QUBITS
Qubit count for simple and GHZ tests. The default is 4.
.TP
.B QFW_RUN_ALL_ITERS
GHZ iteration count. The default is 1.
.TP
.B QFW_RUN_ALL_SHOTS
SuperMarQ shot count. The default is 128.
.TP
.B QFW_RUN_ALL_VQE_ITERS
Qiskit VQE optimizer iterations. The default is 1.
.TP
.B QFW_RUN_ALL_SHIM_LIB
Shim library for the local shim smoke case. Use
.B qrmi
or
.BR qdmi .
.TP
.B QFW_RUN_ALL_CHEM_APP
Chemistry script name. The chemistry case is skipped when this is unset.
.TP
.B QFW_RUN_ALL_TESTS
Default comma-separated selection for
.BR --tests .
.PP
The corresponding
.BR QFW_RUN_ALL_SERVICE_MODE ,
.BR QFW_RUN_ALL_BACKEND ,
.BR QFW_RUN_ALL_SITE_CONFIG ,
and
.B QFW_RUN_ALL_RUNTIME_CONFIG
variables provide defaults for their command options.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run three short NWQSim tests with application-owned services:
.EX
salloc --nodes=1 --ntasks=1 --time=00:30:00
source /opt/openqse/qfw/current/bin/qfw-activate \e
  --venv /opt/openqse/qfw/venv
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_run_all.sh --service-mode local --backend nwqsim \e
  --tests init-test,qiskit-simple,ghz-qiskit
qfw-deactivate
.EE
.PP
Run the compatible suite against a site-owned NWQSim QPM:
.EX
source /opt/openqse/qfw/current/bin/qfw-activate \e
  --venv /opt/openqse/qfw/venv
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_run_all.sh --service-mode site --backend nwqsim
qfw-deactivate
.EE
.PP
Run one bounded SuperMarQ workload against a site-owned IQM QPM:
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
QFW_RUN_ALL_QUBITS=2 QFW_RUN_ALL_SHOTS=16 \e
  ./qfw_run_all.sh --service-mode site --backend iqm \e
  --tests supermarq
.EE
.SH RESULTS
Logs and per-test JSONL files are written beneath
.IR QFW_RUN_BASE_DIR/examples-run-timestamp .
The combined machine-readable report is
.IR summary.jsonl .
